       "Concentration units: mass percent, volume percent, ppm (parts per million).",
       "Mole fraction x = n/N (moles of solute/total moles) — unitless, temperature independent.",
       "Molality m = moles of solute/kg of solvent; molarity M = moles of solute/L of solution.",
       "Molality and mole fraction are temperature independent (mass based); molarity depends on temperature (volume changes).",
       "Henry's law: P = K_H·x — gas solubility ∝ pressure; a soda bottle is an example.",
       "Raoult's law (volatile liquids): P = P°·x; ideal solutions have ΔH_mix = 0, ΔV_mix = 0.",
       "Positive deviation: P_observed > ideal (ΔH > 0); negative deviation: P_observed < ideal (ΔH < 0).",
       "Azeotrope: a mixture of constant boiling point — not separable by fractional distillation (ethanol-water 95.6%).",
       "Colligative properties depend on particle count: vapour-pressure lowering, boiling-point elevation, freezing-point depression, osmotic pressure.",
       "Freezing-point depression ΔT_f = K_f·m; boiling-point elevation ΔT_b = K_b·m.",
       "Osmotic pressure π = CRT (van't Hoff equation) — proportional to moles of solute.",
       "Osmosis: solvent flows through a semipermeable membrane from dilute to concentrated solution.",
       "Reverse osmosis (pressure > π) desalinates sea water.",
       "Isotonic solutions have equal osmotic pressure; 0.9% NaCl is isotonic with blood (used in IV drips).",
       "Van't Hoff factor i = observed/calculated colligative property; i > 1 for dissociation, i < 1 for association.",
