       "d-block: last electron in the (n−1)d orbital; variable oxidation states due to incomplete d-orbitals — e.g. Fe (+2, +3), Mn (+2 to +7).",
       "Coloured ions: due to d−d electronic transitions in incomplete d-orbitals (Cu²⁺ blue); purple colour of MnO4⁻ is from charge transfer.",
       "Paramagnetism arises from unpaired electrons; magnetic moment μ = √[n(n+2)] BM (spin-only formula, n = unpaired e⁻).",
       "KMnO4 is a strong oxidiser: in acidic medium MnO4⁻ → Mn²⁺ (purple colour disappears); K2Cr2O7 is orange, reduced to green Cr³⁺.",
       "Lanthanoid contraction: regular decrease in size due to poor shielding by 4f electrons — so Zr and Hf have nearly identical properties.",
       "Lanthanoids show mainly +3 oxidation state; actinoids are radioactive with more variable states; used in misch metal alloys.",
       "d-block: last electron enters the (n−1)d orbital; four series — 3d (Sc–Zn), 4d, 5d, 6d.",
       "Zn, Cd, Hg have complete d¹⁰, so they are not called transition elements (still d-block).",
       "Variable oxidation states: (n−1)d and ns energies are close — Fe (+2, +3), Mn (+2 to +7).",
       "Paramagnetism: from unpaired d-electrons; μ = √[n(n+2)] BM (n = unpaired e⁻).",
       "Coloured ions: from d-d electronic transitions; Cu²⁺ blue, MnO₄⁻ purple, Cr₂O₇²⁻ orange.",
       "Excellent catalysts: Fe (Haber's process), Ni (hydrogenation), V₂O₅ (Contact process), Pt/Pd.",
       "Tendency to form complexes: vacant d-orbitals available for ligands.",
       "Interstitial compounds: small atoms like H, B, C, N in the lattice — hard, high melting points.",
       "Alloys: brass (Cu-Zn), bronze (Cu-Sn), steel (Fe-C).",
       "K₂Cr₂O₇ is orange, a strong oxidiser: Cr₂O₇²⁻ + 14H⁺ + 6e⁻ → 2Cr³⁺ + 7H₂O (acidic).",
       "KMnO₄ is purple: in acid MnO₄⁻ + 8H⁺ + 5e⁻ → Mn²⁺ + 4H₂O; in alkali MnO₄²⁻ (green); neutral gives MnO₂.",
       "Lanthanoids: 4f fills up (Ce–Lu); common oxidation state +3.",
       "Lanthanoid contraction: steady size decrease due to poor shielding by 4f electrons.",
       "Consequence of lanthanoid contraction: Zr/Hf (4d/5d) have nearly identical sizes and chemistry.",
       "Actinoids: 5f series (Th–Lr); all radioactive; show more variable oxidation states.",
       "Unusual stable states: Eu²⁺, Yb²⁺ (f⁷, f¹⁴), Ce⁴⁺ (f⁰).",
       "Misch metal: lanthanoid alloy — lighter flints, jet engines.",
       "d-block elements have high melting/boiling points; Hg is the exception — liquid at room temperature.",
       "CrO₃, Mn₂O₇ are acidic oxides; MnO is basic — acidic nature rises with oxidation state."
